(N'WF-SE-DISC-01-P-SE-01',N'WF-SE-DISC-01',N'PH-WF-SE-DISC-01-01',2,N'Build the grounded technical discovery brief',NULL,NULL,N'Using the selected approved customer and technical sources, prepare for [meeting]. Summarize known outcomes, decisions, constraints, architecture context, open technical questions and missing evidence. Propose five discovery questions that advance the technical decision. Separate sourced facts from hypotheses.',N'Technical discovery brief with questions and evidence gaps.',N'SE validates the sources, technical context and whether each question is appropriate.',NULL,NULL),
(N'WF-SE-DISC-01-P-SE-02',N'WF-SE-DISC-01',N'PH-WF-SE-DISC-01-01',1,N'Rehearse the technical discovery conversation',NULL,NULL,N'Role-play [customer or stakeholder] for the upcoming technical discovery conversation. Use the approved brief only. Simulate realistic questions and objections, coach clarity and listening, and identify statements requiring technical or customer validation. Do not invent customer facts.',N'Role-play, coaching observations and improvement actions.',N'SE verifies facts, claims and commitments and decides what to change.',NULL,NULL),
(N'WF-SE-ARCH-01-P-SE-01',N'WF-SE-ARCH-01',N'PH-WF-SE-ARCH-01-01',1,N'Compare architecture options and evidence',NULL,NULL,N'Research [architecture decision] using current authoritative Microsoft and approved customer sources. Compare viable options against [decision criteria], identify assumptions, risks, dependencies and evidence gaps, and cite each material claim.',N'Sourced architecture options assessment.',N'SE and architecture SMEs validate current guidance, applicability and unsupported assumptions.',NULL,NULL),
(N'WF-SE-ARCH-01-P-SE-02',N'WF-SE-ARCH-01',N'PH-WF-SE-ARCH-01-01',2,N'Create the architecture decision record',NULL,NULL,N'Using the approved discovery brief and architecture evidence, create a decision record with customer outcome, options considered, criteria, selected direction, risks, dependencies, validation steps, unresolved questions and next technical action.',N'Architecture decision record.',N'SE validates architecture, security, operations, feasibility and customer commitments.',NULL,NULL),
(N'WF-SE-DEMO-01-P-SE-01',N'WF-SE-DEMO-01',N'PH-WF-SE-DEMO-01-02',1,N'Build the demo or workshop plan',NULL,NULL,N'Create a demo or workshop package for [customer decision]. Include audience, scenario, decision criteria, agenda, demo flow, sample data needs, roles, likely objections, tenant or permission dependencies, fallback plan and explicit next decision.',N'Demo or workshop package.',N'SE validates the environment, permissions, technical behavior, evidence and customer appropriateness.',NULL,NULL),
(N'WF-SE-DEMO-01-P-SE-02',N'WF-SE-DEMO-01',N'PH-WF-SE-DEMO-01-01',2,N'Research supporting proof and objections',NULL,NULL,N'Find current authoritative evidence for [scenario or capability]. Return only claims relevant to the customer decision, likely objections, known limitations and SME-needed flags. Cite sources.',N'Evidence and objection brief.',N'SE validates freshness and applicability before customer use.',NULL,NULL),
(N'WF-SE-POC-01-P-SE-01',N'WF-SE-POC-01',N'PH-WF-SE-POC-01-01',1,N'Scope the smallest useful proof',NULL,NULL,N'Create a PoC plan for [technical decision]. Define hypothesis, in-scope scenario, success and exit criteria, milestones, data and environment needs, roles, risks, dependencies, review gates, final decision and handoff if successful.',N'PoC plan and decision gates.',N'SE confirms scope, resources, security, feasibility and that the PoC is necessary.',NULL,NULL),
(N'WF-SE-POC-01-P-SE-02',N'WF-SE-POC-01',N'PH-WF-SE-POC-01-01',2,N'Pressure-test PoC readiness',NULL,NULL,N'Review this PoC plan. Identify vague success criteria, unowned dependencies, unrealistic milestones, missing security or data assumptions, weak linkage to the customer decision and unclear exit paths. Return five review questions and the smallest revisions needed.',N'Readiness review and revision list.',N'SE owns the go or no-go decision and confirms all required reviewers.',NULL,NULL),
(N'WF-SE-DEAL-01-P-SE-01',N'WF-SE-DEAL-01',N'PH-WF-SE-DEAL-01-01',1,N'Inspect technical deal health',NULL,NULL,N'Review [opportunity] and summarize the intended customer decision, current technical stage, exit criteria, proof completed, open blockers, recent technical engagement, missing roles and next recommended technical action. Show the source signal and flag unavailable context.',N'Technical deal-health brief.',N'SE validates MSX accuracy, customer context, technical risk and the next action.',NULL,NULL),
